# --- Kalponik ---
# Readest's service defaults above are blanked so no build can reach Readest's
# backend. PostHog and Stripe: empty (no key, no PostHog; no payments). Supabase:
# obviously fake placeholders (https://example.supabase.co, "placeholder-anon-key")
# because supabase-js throws on an empty URL and many tests import the client.
# Real values come from .env.local (dev) and the server's .env (production).
# The Kalponik build flags (self-hosted, no updater) live in .env.web and
# .env.tauri, which every build and dev script loads. They stay out of this
# file because the test script loads only .env, and Kalponik's tests expect the
# upstream defaults (paid-plan gates, updater on).
